# Front end
- Treat `src/` as source of truth when it exists. Rebuild with `bun x vite build`; do not directly patch generated/minified assets as the normal workflow.
- Keep `src/main.js` focused on imports/initialization; split functionality into `src/scripts/` incrementally, one feature at a time.
- Initialize page-specific features only where needed; use page type and DOM existence checks. Dynamic import is welcome when it clearly reduces unnecessary loading.
- Keep CSS in the responsible partial/module instead of stacking permanent patches at the end of a global file.
- Verify a selector is unused across PHP/JS before deleting it.
- Do not apply `text-align:center` broadly to article content. Keep body text naturally left-aligned while media/embeds/cards fit the content width.
- Do not cause mobile horizontal scrolling.
- Do not use JS as a post-layout correction when CSS can solve the problem.
- Avoid `!important` unless compatibility genuinely requires it.
- Filled brand pills/badges/chips/FAB/series banners retain white text/icons unless the user explicitly approves a visual change.
- Preserve initialization order when dependencies exist.